{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsqLb5GSnR8dKn7EsVo1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex call as the `codex` lane under `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way the kimi lane does. The lane has not produced a real graded answer yet, because `CODEX_API_KEY` isn't set on this machine.\n\n**What the lane does**\n- Runs `codex exec` with the same flags as the `codex` lane, inside `sandbox-exec` with a scratch `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME`. The real `~/.codex` is not visible, so `auth.json` and the MCP servers are not loaded.\n- Logs in with `CODEX_API_KEY` from the environment, and exits 2 if it's unset.\n- Writes `-o` into a scratch folder in `/tmp`, copies `final.txt` into the run folder after the sandbox exits, then deletes the scratch folder.\n- Marks a run as failed (exit 1) if it exits 0 but `final.txt` is missing or empty.\n\nI also added the lane to the README. `sandbox/agent.sb` and the existing lanes are unchanged.\n\n**Colleague's note**\n- Applied: the scratch-folder fix for `-o`, the check that the answer file exists rather than trusting the exit code, and keeping stdout/stderr redirects outside the sandbox.\n- Applied in principle only: the failure needs the run folder under the real home. Here the repo is outside `$HOME`, so the premise doesn't show up in this checkout. The README places the eval repo under `$HOME` on the eval Mac, where it would apply. I did not run from there.\n- Not applied: grepping stderr for \"Operation not permitted\" as a failure signal. The agent's own shell can hit denied writes legitimately, so I used the `final.txt` check instead.\n- Not applicable: Mistral Vibe, since this harness has no Vibe lane.\n\n**How I checked it**\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- The profile denies writes under `$HOME` and allows writes under `/tmp`.\n- With a stub `codex` on `PATH`, the success case copies `final.txt` and returns 0, a missing answer file returns 1, and a missing key returns 2.\n- The real Codex binary, run against a closed local port with a dummy key, starts under the profile and makes no denied writes. The first try failed because `CODEX_HOME` must exist; the stub had hidden that, so I added the `mkdir`. Codex's request reached `api.openai.com` and was rejected with a 401 before any prompt was sent, because `OPENAI_BASE_URL` was ignored.\n\n**Trade-offs**\n- The key lives in an environment variable, which the agent's shell can read. The sandbox doesn't hide it.\n- The sandboxed run uses Codex's defaults. The real config pins no model, but the sandboxed run skips its MCP servers.\n\n**Still to do:** run `CODEX_API_KEY=... ./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` once to confirm a real answer comes through. I did not commit anything. `run.sh`, `README.md`, and the new `ANSWER.md` are in the working tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":63878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":301},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ab982a0-28fb-4132-a1bb-c117bdbd77f2","uuid":"7780bc80-a35b-4be4-bfb8-9377d0a1a15f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:33:34.197Z","request_id":"req_011CgsqLas7HkbTzR3crNwei"}
